WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.934
This is PreFlight, an AI testing application for deployed websites. The

00:00:04.934 --> 00:00:09.868
problem is simple: a user interface can look successful while the

00:00:09.868 --> 00:00:14.802
underlying workflow is broken. PreFlight combines browser interaction, application evidence, and

00:00:14.802 --> 00:00:19.735
configured database expectations. This demonstration uses the real deployed application and

00:00:19.735 --> 00:00:24.669
a deliberately broken waitlist. Any time spent waiting for cloud processing

00:00:24.669 --> 00:00:26.912
is shortened in this recording.

00:00:28.412 --> 00:00:32.483
Here is the example. I enter an email address and click

00:00:32.483 --> 00:00:36.554
Join the waitlist. The email disappears, and a toast says, You

00:00:36.554 --> 00:00:40.625
have entered the waitlist. To a visitor, the action appears successful.

00:00:40.625 --> 00:00:44.696
But the submit handler never calls the waitlist API. The database

00:00:44.696 --> 00:00:48.767
remains empty. This is an intentional persistence bug, not a database

00:00:48.767 --> 00:00:52.468
connection error. Looking only at the toast would miss it.

00:00:53.968 --> 00:00:58.195
A judge opens a separate invitation and receives an isolated guest

00:00:58.195 --> 00:01:02.422
workspace, without signing in to GitHub. The secure guest cookie identifies

00:01:02.422 --> 00:01:06.649
that session. Other guests and the sponsor's personal projects remain inaccessible.

00:01:06.649 --> 00:01:10.875
The example project already has a read-only database verification configured. The

00:01:10.875 --> 00:01:15.102
check looks for the unique email marker submitted during this run.

00:01:15.102 --> 00:01:19.329
I select the workflow and start the swarm. No per-user run

00:01:19.329 --> 00:01:21.635
quota is enabled for this pilot.

00:01:23.134 --> 00:01:27.716
The persistence contract requires more than an AI opinion. The browser

00:01:27.716 --> 00:01:32.299
must submit the current unique marker and observe a newly displayed

00:01:32.299 --> 00:01:36.881
success message. The read-only query must then fail its expected row

00:01:36.881 --> 00:01:41.464
count. A fresh browser context repeats the interaction with a different

00:01:41.464 --> 00:01:46.046
marker. Only when both accepted submissions fail their database expectations does

00:01:46.046 --> 00:01:50.629
this path confirm a persistence defect. Invalid input, an old toast,

00:01:50.629 --> 00:01:54.794
or a cloud service failure cannot establish the same conclusion.

00:01:56.294 --> 00:02:01.407
The architecture separates the web application, background workers, and browser execution.

00:02:01.407 --> 00:02:06.520
Next.js on Vercel authorizes the project and run. Trigger manages the

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:11.634
agents. Neon stores persistent projects and reports. Browser requests pass through

00:02:11.634 --> 00:02:16.747
a restricted network policy. A Vercel Sandbox fallback runs Chromium in

00:02:16.747 --> 00:02:21.860
a disposable virtual machine with outbound access denied and without production

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:26.973
database, GitHub, or model credentials. Source investigation uses a separately authorized

00:02:26.973 --> 00:02:32.086
broker and a pinned repository commit. Evidence and uncertainty stay visible

00:02:32.086 --> 00:02:33.481
in the report.

00:02:34.994 --> 00:02:40.082
The public repository includes the system design, local setup, automated checks,

00:02:40.082 --> 00:02:45.171
and deployment history. The submission resources also describe the target customer,

00:02:45.171 --> 00:02:50.259
distribution plan, and financial assumptions. Proposed pricing is clearly labeled; real

00:02:50.259 --> 00:02:55.347
payment activation is still pending. The pilot demonstrates the central user

00:02:55.347 --> 00:03:00.436
loop: connect an app, run a workflow, and inspect evidence about

00:03:00.436 --> 00:03:05.524
what actually happened. This narration is synthetic. The application screens and

00:03:05.524 --> 00:03:07.374
recorded interactions are real.
